      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "No assigned numerical exercise. Exact SI offset273.15=5463/20 cancels in final-minus-initial differences. Reviewer probes:20C=5863/20K and35-20C=15K. The absolute ratio for40C versus20C is6263/5863, not2; absolute200to400K has ratio2. State-function differences telescope to zero on a closed cycle. Boundary classifications were read conceptually, not certified by a zero-valued test: closed forbids matter crossing but permits energy transfer; isolated forbids both. Constructed energy change11-7=4J illustrates an allowed closed-system exchange.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Choose the matter/energy boundary first. Closed gas has no matter crossing; isolated additionally has no energy exchange. Unchanged contents alone do not prove isolation. Equilibrium simple gas at fixed composition has definedp,V,T; state-function changes need endpoints. Thermal contact permits heat exchange. Celsius/kelvin offset is exact; ordinary gas absolute temperatures are positive and denominators in ratios nonzero.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Boundary selection precedes closed/open/isolated classification and state variables. Distinguishes heat from work and temperature from energy, then teaches exact offset versus temperature differences before ratios. The historical assisted-review flag is ignored as evidence; all blocks were read.",
