      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "Momentum-flux pressure with isotropic translational energy givespV=NkT, thenN=nNA givesnRT. PrintedR8.314=4157/500 is a rounded tabulated working coefficient, not exactSI. NA*kB=207861565453831/25000000000000; rounding to0.001 gives8.314, with explicit nonzero gap11565453831/25000000000000. No source calculation demands precision beyond the printed coefficient. Reviewer probe:n1/10mol,T250K,p100000Pa gives4157/2000000m³=4157/2000L using that workingR, with no hidden rounding of the computed result. Two-state ratios cancelnR only for fixed gas amount; leaks change n. The source SVG rectangles78*126=234*42=9828px² check constantpV without inventing physical axis scales.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Classical dilute ideal gas, equilibrium states, positive absoluteT,V,n and absolute pressure. Fixed quantity/composition is required for two-state ratios; otherwise change n explicitly. The source excludes molecular size/interactions and warns about condensation. PrintedR is the conventional rounded working value; no exactSI or higher-precision numerical result is claimed. Exact arithmetic within an assigned rounded coefficient is distinguished from physical constant exactness. Gauge pressure needs the atmospheric contribution.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Absolute variables and SI units precede two-state ratios; n is held constant only where justified. Explicit manometer warning and ideal-gas limits. The tabulated constant is checked at working precision without silently equating it to exactSI. No false computed rounded identity or calculator requirement.",
